course: dictionary
lesson: 1770
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning is right. Clerk is a good example.
explain: «The Clerk adds it up: twelve months for the theft, three years for the driving.» Someone is adding up sentences in a court, so here a clerk is an official who keeps the records for a court.
explain: «The clerk laughs: "you're obstructing the other passengers".» Someone is speaking to a traveller, so this clerk works at a station and serves people. Ask yourself who is talking and where they are.
fact: A clerk is a person whose job is keeping records, filing and writing in an office.
fact: In the US and Canada, a clerk can also be a shop assistant who serves customers.
fact: A court clerk or town clerk is an official in charge of records for a court, council or school.
fact: Phrases to know: bank clerk, desk clerk, sales clerk, court clerk, town clerk.
fact: To check a meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The Clerk adds it up: twelve months for the theft, three years for the driving.» What job does the clerk do here? | Cooks meals in a kitchen | Sells fruit at a market | Drives the buses in town | *Keeps the records for a court
exercise: In a shop, Sam asks the clerk where the batteries are. What does clerk mean here? | A bird that sings in trees | A person who files papers in a court | *A shop assistant who helps customers | A teacher in a school hall
exercise: «The clerk laughs: "you're obstructing the other passengers".» What does obstructing mean? | Sleeping | *Blocking | Helping | Singing
test: What does a town clerk do? | *Keeps the records for the town council | Sells bread in a bakery | Drives the buses | Cleans the streets
test: A desk clerk at a hotel gives you your room key. What does desk clerk mean here? | *A person working at the front desk | A teacher | A pilot | A cook
exam: Why do we check the clues around a word like clerk? | Because clerk is always spelled the same way | Because dictionaries never help | *Because clerk can have more than one meaning, and the context shows which one is meant | Because clerk only means one thing
